From fb8c7ce5ce5cd4bbac15455f1ff3ef941486bc78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sandeep Tomer <stomer@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:45:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplMesh: monitor: keep AP Metrics responsive and allow local
 STA ARP control

Replace the 300 ms blocking scan-trigger retry delay with a Monitor
event-loop timer. Preserve pending parameters, reject overlapping requests,
and cancel pending retries during abort and shutdown. Explicitly invalidate
the timer handle after cancellation so subsequent requests can arm retries.
Abort pending work and report initial trigger failure if a retry timer
cannot be created.

Refresh cumulative station traffic counters through the HAL when preparing
AP Metrics. Use a separate response snapshot to preserve periodic polling
deltas and RSSI measurements, with cached fallback on read failure. Reuse
snapshots for duplicate BSSIDs and use them for MLO per-link traffic TLVs.
Emit one timestamped counter trace per station during response preparation.
Expose the existing measurement-window poll count in Agent configuration.

Prefer native 64-bit TX/RX byte counters using the stable nl80211 ABI IDs
RX=23 and TX=24. Include both IDs in parser bounds, supporting headers that
omit the enum names without preprocessor checks or macro shadowing. Extend
32-bit-only counters across rollover before AP Metrics unit conversion.
Fallback totals belong to one association; reads must be less than 4 GiB
apart and cannot distinguish an unannounced driver reset from rollover.

Read monitor_disable_initiative_arp as an optional local Agent override.
Keep the generated default at 0 so automatic STA probing remains enabled
under Controller policy. The test team can set the local option to 1 to
disable automatic probes and prevent Controller updates from re-enabling
them. Preserve ARP for explicit RSSI requests.

Signed-off-by: Sandeep Tomer <stomer@qti.qualcomm.com>
